# API DTOs

## Paths

- Requests: `src/dtos/req/<domain>.req.ts`
- Responses: `src/dtos/res/<domain>.res.ts`

## Naming

- Request body types end with **`Payload`** — e.g. `RegisterPayload`, `LoginPayload`.
- Response body / `dataModel` types end with **`Response`** — e.g. `RegisterResponse`, `LoginResponse`.
- Nested objects used only inside a payload may use descriptive names (e.g. `RegisterSitePayload`) and still live in the same `*.req.ts` file.

## Unknown responses

If Swagger (or the API) does not define a response schema, still export a named type:

```ts
export type RegisterResponse = unknown;
```

Use it in services: `axiosInstance.post<ApiResponse<RegisterResponse>>(...)`.

## Services

- Import payloads/responses from `@/dtos/...`, not ad-hoc inline shapes.
- Paths are relative to axios `baseURL` (`…/api`), e.g. `POST /Auth/register` → `axiosInstance.post("/Auth/register", payload)`.
